Design a premium, modern, highly interactive website for an Indian engineering laboratory and educational equipment manufacturer called “Ambros INDIA”.

REFERENCE DIRECTION:
Take inspiration from the immersive, experimental and editorial web experience of Active Theory (activetheory.net), especially:
- Large typography
- Strong visual storytelling
- Scroll-driven transitions
- Full-width visual sections
- Interactive category navigation
- Large product/project imagery
- Smooth motion and micro-interactions
- Minimal but distinctive navigation
- A website that feels like an experience rather than a conventional catalogue

IMPORTANT:
Do NOT copy Active Theory’s dark visual style.
Create a LIGHT, BRIGHT, PREMIUM INDUSTRIAL/ENGINEERING aesthetic.

BRAND CHARACTER:
Ambros India should feel:
- Engineering-driven
- Precise
- Innovative
- Trustworthy
- Educational
- Industrial
- Premium
- Modern Indian engineering company
- Suitable for universities, engineering colleges, laboratories, institutions and industrial training centres

COLOR DIRECTION:
Primary background: warm white / off-white
Secondary background: very light cool grey
Primary text: deep charcoal / near-black
Accent color: sophisticated engineering blue
Secondary accent: subtle orange or copper
Use colors sparingly.

Avoid:
- Full dark backgrounds
- Neon cyberpunk aesthetics
- Excessive gradients
- Glassmorphism everywhere
- Generic corporate blue website look
- Stock-photo-heavy layouts

TYPOGRAPHY:
Use a modern geometric sans-serif such as:
Inter / Manrope / Satoshi / Neue Montreal style.

Large bold editorial typography.
Headings should be oversized and confident.
Body typography should remain clean and highly readable.

WEBSITE STRUCTURE:

1. HERO SECTION

Create a dramatic full-screen hero section.

Top navigation:
Ambros INDIA logo on left.

Navigation:
PRODUCTS
LABS
ABOUT
APPLICATIONS
RESOURCES
CONTACT

Right side:
Search icon
Menu / navigation button

Hero headline:

“ENGINEERING
THE WAY
YOU LEARN.”

Alternative small supporting text:
“Laboratory equipment, engineering apparatus and educational models for the next generation of engineers.”

Hero visual:
Use a premium hyper-realistic photograph/render of an engineering laboratory environment containing:
- Mechanical laboratory equipment
- Thermodynamics apparatus
- Fluid mechanics equipment
- Structural testing equipment
- Automobile engineering equipment
- Engineering models

Make the equipment highly detailed and realistic.

The hero should have subtle motion:
- Slow parallax
- Equipment subtly moving as the user scrolls
- Typography entering with smooth animation
- Image transitioning as the page scrolls

Add a small scroll indicator:
EXPLORE Ambros ↓


2. CATEGORY EXPERIENCE

Create a large editorial section titled:

“EXPLORE OUR ENGINEERING WORLD”

Instead of traditional small product cards, create large horizontal/vertical interactive category panels.

The main categories are:

01
THEORY OF MACHINE LAB

02
FLUID MECHANICS LAB

03
HEAT TRANSFER LAB

04
THERMODYNAMICS LAB

05
STRUCTURAL MECHANICS LAB

06
ENGINEERING APPARATUS,
MODELS & CHARTS

07
AUTOMOBILE ENGINEERING
& I.C. ENGINE LAB

Each category should have:
- Large category number
- Large typography
- High-quality engineering equipment image
- Short description
- “Explore Lab →” CTA

Interaction:
When the cursor moves over a category:
- Image expands
- Background subtly changes
- Category number animates
- Text shifts slightly
- Arrow moves
- Image has subtle zoom/parallax

Keep the interface clean and premium.


3. FEATURED LAB EXPERIENCE

Create a large immersive section for:

“BUILT FOR
REAL ENGINEERING.”

Show a large engineering laboratory photograph/render.

Overlay small technical labels around equipment, similar to an engineering schematic.

Example labels:

MECHANICAL SYSTEMS
FLOW ANALYSIS
THERMAL TRANSFER
MATERIAL TESTING
AUTOMOTIVE SYSTEMS

Use thin technical lines connecting labels to the equipment.

Keep the design elegant rather than overly futuristic.


4. PRODUCT DISCOVERY SECTION

Title:

“FROM CONCEPT
TO EXPERIMENT.”

Create an interactive product discovery grid.

Categories:

LABORATORY EQUIPMENT
ENGINEERING MODELS
DEMONSTRATION APPARATUS
WALL CHARTS
TRAINING EQUIPMENT
AUTOMOBILE LAB EQUIPMENT

Each card should use a large product image and minimal text.

On hover:
Image zooms slightly.
Product name slides upward.
CTA appears.

Use generous whitespace.


5. ABOUT Ambros INDIA

Create a clean editorial split-screen section.

Left:
Large heading:

“ENGINEERING
KNOWLEDGE,
MADE TANGIBLE.”

Right:
Short company introduction.

Example:

“Ambros India develops laboratory equipment, engineering apparatus, educational models and training systems designed to make engineering concepts easier to understand, demonstrate and apply.”

Include a CTA:
ABOUT Ambros INDIA →


6. ENGINEERING APPLICATIONS

Create a horizontal scrolling section titled:

“WHERE ENGINEERING
COMES TO LIFE.”

Show applications:

MECHANICAL ENGINEERING
AUTOMOBILE ENGINEERING
CIVIL ENGINEERING
THERMAL ENGINEERING
FLUID MECHANICS
ENGINEERING EDUCATION

Use high-quality images of real laboratory environments.

Each application should feel like a visual story rather than a normal service card.


7. WHY Ambros

Create a clean numbered section:

01
ENGINEERING PRECISION

02
EDUCATIONAL FOCUS

03
ROBUST CONSTRUCTION

04
PRACTICAL LEARNING

05
INSTITUTIONAL SUPPORT

Use large numbers and minimal text.

Visual style should resemble a premium engineering publication.


