LAYOUT & INTERACTION:

Desktop:
1440px wide design.
Use a 12-column grid.
Generous whitespace.
Large typography.
Full-width imagery.
Editorial layouts.

Mobile:
Create a responsive 390px mobile version.
Use stacked category sections.
Large touch-friendly navigation.
Horizontal swipe galleries where appropriate.
Keep animations subtle and performant.

ANIMATION DIRECTION:

Use:
- Scroll-triggered reveals
- Image parallax
- Smooth category transitions
- Horizontal scrolling sections
- Typography masking
- Image scale transitions
- Hover image zoom
- Number animations
- Subtle cursor interaction

Do NOT make animations distracting.

The website should feel:
“An engineering exhibition on the web.”

DESIGN LANGUAGE:

Think:
Apple product presentation
+
premium engineering catalogue
+
modern architecture magazine
+
interactive digital exhibition

But maintain a distinctly Indian engineering/manufacturing identity.

IMPORTANT DESIGN PRINCIPLE:

This is NOT a traditional B2B engineering website.

Do not create:
- Generic hero slider
- Typical Bootstrap cards
- Crowded navigation
- Huge paragraphs
- Old-fashioned catalogue layout
- Excessive icons
- Generic stock photos

Instead create an immersive visual journey where users discover Ambros India's laboratory categories through large imagery, typography and interaction.

PRIMARY USER JOURNEY:

HOME
↓
EXPLORE LABS
↓
SELECT ENGINEERING CATEGORY
↓
VIEW LAB
↓
EXPLORE EQUIPMENT
↓
VIEW TECHNICAL DETAILS
↓
REQUEST ENQUIRY

Create the complete Figma design system including:
- Desktop homepage
- Mobile homepage
- Category landing page
- Lab detail page
- Product detail page
- Navigation states
- Hover states
- Buttons
- Cards
- Typography system
- Color system
- Responsive components
- Scroll/interaction states

Overall visual impression:
LIGHT.
PREMIUM.
ENGINEERING.
PRECISE.
IMMERSIVE.
MODERN.
INDUSTRIAL.
EDUCATIONAL.

The final result should look like a next-generation engineering equipment website, not a conventional industrial catalogue.